hush: exp_word starts as NULL, not as itself

expand_one_var() initialized exp_word to itself to quiet "may be used uninitialized", and GCC 15
warns that it is used uninitialized instead (-Wuninitialized). It is set wherever it is read:
every exp_op other than 0 and 'L' comes from the branch that sets it (BMDS).

--- a/shell/hush.c
+++ b/shell/hush.c
@@ -6639,7 +6639,7 @@
 	char exp_op;
 	char exp_save = exp_save; /* for compiler */
 	char *exp_saveptr; /* points to expansion operator */
-	char *exp_word = exp_word; /* for compiler */
+	char *exp_word = NULL; /* BMDS: set wherever it's read (exp_op not 0 or 'L'); GCC 15 flags x = x */
 	char arg0;
 
 	val = NULL;
